NPA's Physical AI Data Factory workflows are NPA-native adaptations informed by
two official NVIDIA repositories with distinct roles:

  https://github.com/NVIDIA/physical-ai-data-factory
  revision e4c663cbbdcf159ad952751274c883c81d3ab4be
  documentation and skills: CC-BY-4.0; source code: Apache-2.0

This is NVIDIA's PAIDF ecosystem entry point. At the recorded revision it
publishes agent skills for Defect Image Generation and Video Data Augmentation,
run upstream through NVIDIA OSMO, and links to the reusable PAIDF component
repositories.

  https://github.com/NVIDIA/paidf-orchestration
  revision f7ecd8c5d7aeec28b2d476b9e71b53a48ba8c0f9
  source code: Apache-2.0

This is NVIDIA's separate Airflow-on-Kubernetes scaled orchestrator. At the
recorded revision it publishes Image Attribute Augmentation and Event Video
Generation DAGs. It is not the implementation repository for the upstream VDA
skill and it is not embedded or executed by NPA.

NPA keeps `npa.workflow/v0.0.1` as the authoring surface and SkyPilot as its sole
execution engine. It does not vendor OSMO, Airflow, either repository, PAIDF NGC
service images, model weights, or input datasets. The shipped workflow set is:

  physical-ai-data-factory.yaml              direct VDA translation
  paidf-defect-image-generation.yaml         direct DIG Day-1 manual-ROI translation
  paidf-image-attribute-augmentation.yaml    direct Airflow IAA translation
  paidf-event-video-generation.yaml          direct Airflow EVG translation
  paidf-cosmos3.yaml                         NPA-specific Cosmos3 VDA alternative

Executable component sources are independently pinned:

  https://github.com/NVIDIA/paidf-augmentation
  revision bc5719362492a1e3b40bd7d33b43c46dd89efad5 (Apache-2.0)

  https://github.com/NVIDIA/paidf-auto-labeling
  revision 36dc1114dea00d9986df97325a664520993964de (Apache-2.0)

  https://github.com/NVIDIA/paidf-anomalygen
  revision dbaf7d7d9003f048230f9026da5969e9e5931785 (Apache-2.0)

  https://github.com/NVIDIA/paidf-simulation
  revision 498751aceeea3dc3bac0d5fb043bf3553aec46a6 (Apache-2.0; ecosystem
  attribution only for the scoped manual-ROI DIG translation)

  https://github.com/NVIDIA/paidf-curation-and-retrieval
  revision 02079bbd272900c837ebdbd0bf44384dfdf1f25e (Apache-2.0)

Vendor runtime images are referenced by immutable registry digest and are not
claimed as NPA-published images. NVIDIA's AnomalyGen image fails SkyPilot
bootstrap, so the checked-in restricted `paidf-anomalygen-sky` image builds the
exact Apache-2.0 source revision on digest-pinned public CUDA bases. It belongs
in an operator-controlled registry and may never be published to NPA's public
GHCR namespace without a separate redistribution review. NPA runtime-fetches exact
Apache-2.0 protocol source where the selected vendor service image does not
carry its client, and verifies the fetched commit before execution. All
registered components use S3-compatible object storage for handoffs.
Each run writes `reports/upstream.json` (`npa.paidf.upstream.v1`) so this
adaptation boundary and the exact public revisions travel with its artifacts.

Runtime model snapshots are also pinned and remain outside published images:

  Qwen/Qwen-Image-Edit-2511
  revision 6f3ccc0b56e431dc6a0c2b2039706d7d26f22cb9

  nvidia/Cosmos3-Super-Image2Video
  revision 4f847566f3d3388fbf0ac07b99dd1a6432db9ecd

Gated weights remain runtime fetches under the operator's own upstream identity.
Access credentials prove fetch authorization, not permission to redistribute
weights. See `skills/NOTICE-NVIDIA-COSMOS-OSS` and
`skills/NOTICE-NVIDIA-COSMOS3` for the executable component boundaries.

